{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/HeavyLightDecomposition"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Decomposes an arborescence. O(n).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"arborescence","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","text":"Arborescence","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Trees12ArborescenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14TreeAlgorithms23HeavyLightDecompositionVyACyxG5Trees12ArborescenceVyxGcfc","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Arborescence","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Trees12ArborescenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">)"}],"symbolKind":"init","roleHeading":"Initializer","modules":[{"name":"TreeAlgorithms"}],"title":"init(_:)","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/TreeAlgorithms\/HeavyLightDecomposition.swift#L25","fileName":"HeavyLightDecomposition.swift"}},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/heavylightdecomposition\/init(_:)-7w6b0"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/HeavyLightDecomposition\/init(_:)-7w6b0","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgorithms":{"role":"collection","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms","title":"TreeAlgorithms"},"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgorithms/HeavyLightDecomposition/init(_:)-7w6b0":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/HeavyLightDecomposition\/init(_:)-7w6b0","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Decomposes an arborescence. O(n)."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"init(_:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/heavylightdecomposition\/init(_:)-7w6b0","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Trees12ArborescenceV","text":"Arborescence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}]},"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgorithms/HeavyLightDecomposition":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HeavyLightDecomposition","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The heavy–light decomposition of a rooted tree or arborescence: each vertex’s heavy child is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its child with the largest subtree (the first in "},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order on a tie), and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"heavy edges form paths. Vertices get positions in a preorder that takes the heavy child first,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so each heavy path and each subtree is an interval of positions, and any path between two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices is at most 2⌊log₂ n⌋ + 1 intervals ("},{"code":"segments(from:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), for path and subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queries over a structure indexed by position."}],"url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/heavylightdecomposition","title":"HeavyLightDecomposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/HeavyLightDecomposition","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HeavyLightDecomposition","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Arborescence":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Arborescence","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Arborescence"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent (NetworkX "},{"code":"is_arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Edmonds). A "},{"code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are the children, "},{"code":"predecessors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parent (zero or one), and each edge is "},{"code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Arborescence"}]}}}